{
	title: 'Versioned task blueprint',
	spec: 'A Git repository contains a tasks/ directory with a Tsk format marker (project.ason, with an optional keep list of files that survive a rebuild), a freeform README for shared build context, and flat ID directories with ASON task records. Require spec (not description) for intended behavior and constraints; document optional once: true for one-off work that stays done across rebuilds and notes as a list of observations. The initial records describe Tsk itself and can be read without a working CLI. Lead the root README with a small task object showing title and spec, explain why a task plan lets agents rebuild rather than endlessly patch software, and present the tsk CLI workflow as the main interface. Explain reset (which leaves once: true tasks done, so one-off work such as publishing a release is never repeated), repeatedly fold tasks from tsk foldable into every target and delete them, then implement tasks from tsk ready and finish with tasks/crosscheck against the pre-rebuild commit; keep this algorithm separate from Git checkpoints. Keep ASON storage discoverable without making it the product.',
